1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,100
<i> Go ahead, shoot.</i>

2
00:00:01,233 --> 00:00:02,133
<i> Don't aim at him.</i>

3
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:03,533
<i>That's Andrew Dizon,
a famous vlogger.</i>

4
00:00:03,667 --> 00:00:04,633
<i>All right, Sir,
please come in.</i>

5
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:05,567
<i> Andrew?</i>

6
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:06,633
<i>Yvette, what are you doing here?</i>

7
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,300
<i> I'm here for Hope Circle.</i>

8
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:09,867
<i>What about you,
what are you doing here?</i>

9
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,767
<i>Long story, Yvette.
Anyway, I have to go.</i>

10
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,333
<i> I've got a bonus.</i>

11
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:17,433
<i>I already know where that
leech Golda is hiding.</i>

12
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:20,900
<i>She's here right under my nose.</i>

13
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:21,967
<i> Braggy is here.</i>

14
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,433
<i> Where are you, Golda?</i>

15
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:26,100
<i>Wait, didn't I tell all of you
to step outside?</i>

16
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:28,633
<i>Joey, one of the syndicates
looking for you is here.</i>

17
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:30,800
<i>I'll take all the heavy calibers
in your arsenal</i>

18
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:32,900
<i>as long as the transaction
stays clean.</i>

19
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,267
<i> Because if anything leaks,</i>

20
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:35,600
<i> the deal stops</i>

21
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:37,100
<i> and so does the breathing</i>

22
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:38,400
<i> of whoever starts talking.</i>

23
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:40,033
<i> Don't push me.</i>

24
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:42,800
<i>I might smash that jar
over your head.</i>

25
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:44,500
<i>- It's on.
- I'll handle it.</i>

26
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:46,567
<i>- It's a deal.
- Congrats, boys!</i>

27
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,167
<i>- Braggy...
- Who's this?</i>

28
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,433
<i>Let's just say I know what
you've been cooking up</i>

29
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:51,800
<i> with Godfather.</i>

30
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:53,267
<i>How did someone find out about
our transaction?</i>

31
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,200
<i>You liars!
You're an animal, Godfather!</i>

32
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,233
<i>You're going straight to hell
now!</i>

33
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:57,533
<i> You should go first!</i>

34
00:00:57,667 --> 00:00:59,067
<i>My mother, I need to go to her.</i>

35
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,367
<i> I'll be the one going in.</i>

36
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,500
<i>Andrew wouldn't abandon Mom,
right?</i>

37
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:05,367
<i>After I fill
Braganza with bullets,</i>

38
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,267
<i> you're next.</i>

39
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:09,433
<i>You have nowhere left to run,
Braganza!</i>

40
00:01:09,567 --> 00:01:10,433
<i> Theresa?</i>

41
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:11,833
<i>I can't let Theresa
get away again.</i>

42
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:12,933
<i> I'm going to catch her.</i>

43
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:13,900
<i> We can't get trapped here!</i>

44
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:16,133
<i> Chase that animal!</i>

45
00:01:16,267 --> 00:01:17,133
<i> Miss Clarissa, let's go.</i>

46
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:18,667
<i> Don't let her get out alive!</i>

47
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,667
<i> Find Golda!</i>

48
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:32,367
<i> [OBB]</i>

49
00:01:39,567 --> 00:01:43,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

50
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,867
Be honest.

51
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,233
Were you really going to
leave me at that party?

52
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,133
What do you think?

53
00:01:49,267 --> 00:01:50,133
They were already shooting
at each other.

54
00:01:50,267 --> 00:01:52,400
Do you think I'd still
look for you?

55
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:56,567
I guess there won't be
a next date.

56
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:01,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

57
00:02:01,467 --> 00:02:04,000
What the hell? You idiot!
Are you trying to kill yourself?

58
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:09,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,700
Are you guys sure you're okay?

60
00:02:16,533 --> 00:02:18,567
Miss Clarissa...

61
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,067
why were you at the party today?

62
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,300
She's my assistant.

63
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:23,700
She's with me.

64
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:26,200
Tomas wasn't around,
so I brought her with me.

65
00:02:27,033 --> 00:02:29,367
Oh, why do you know Clarissa?

66
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,333
[♪UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING♪]

67
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:35,167
I did an expose on her husband,

68
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,400
Major Miguel Delgado.

69
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:46,200
Thank you, Boss Idol Andrew.

70
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,233
If you hadn't arrived,

71
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:53,267
I don't know what might have
happened to me.

72
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:56,067
Why did this even happen?

73
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,600
Everything was going fine
at the party earlier,

74
00:02:57,733 --> 00:02:59,967
then suddenly people
started shooting.

75
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:02,200
There could be many reasons,
Yvette.

76
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:04,067
What do you mean?

77
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:07,000
And what were you doing
at the party earlier?

78
00:03:07,133 --> 00:03:09,200
Were you even invited?

79
00:03:09,633 --> 00:03:11,033
I was there for an expose.

80
00:03:11,167 --> 00:03:12,667
But something went wrong,
betrayal,

81
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,567
a turf war,

82
00:03:15,667 --> 00:03:17,433
a deal gone bad.

83
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:20,100
[REVVING]

84
00:03:20,233 --> 00:03:24,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:34,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:47,500
- Who are you?
- Wait...

87
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:48,967
Where's Theresa?

88
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,633
Wait, Theresa?

89
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:52,333
I don't know any Theresa.

90
00:03:52,467 --> 00:03:55,500
Wait, don't you know
Vicente Alcala?

91
00:03:56,067 --> 00:03:58,200
He's an arms dealer,

92
00:03:58,333 --> 00:03:59,633
also known as Godfather.

93
00:03:59,767 --> 00:04:01,133
- What?
- Ah...

94
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:03,600
He sells guns?

95
00:04:05,067 --> 00:04:06,800
Illegally.

96
00:04:06,933 --> 00:04:08,467
It can't be!
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,733
As far as I know, he's a very
successful businessman.

98
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:14,433
That's why I'm trying to get him
as a sponsor

99
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:16,667
for my foundation.

100
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:21,900
Oh my, Ma'am.
That man sounds dangerous.

101
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:25,833
That's why, Yvette,
you should always be careful

102
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:29,867
and examine the people
you deal with.

103
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:34,367
Sometimes, wolves hide
under sheep's clothing.

104
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:38,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,400
The one who was with you,
where is she?

106
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:48,700
She left already.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:04:50,767 --> 00:04:52,733
Her name is Lisa, not Theresa.

108
00:04:52,867 --> 00:04:53,967
Where did she go?

109
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,567
I don't know, promise.

110
00:04:57,367 --> 00:05:01,467
[REVVING]
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:03,533 --> 00:05:05,367
<i> I was worried about you</i>

112
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,367
<i> so I looked for you,</i>

113
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:10,767
<i>and then you just left me there?</i>

114
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,267
<i> That's mean!</i>

115
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:16,333
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:23,700
[PHONE RINGS]

117
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:25,233
<i> Why?</i>

118
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:27,367
<i> I need a ride, right now.</i>

119
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,100
<i> You're leaving me?</i>

120
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:31,700
<i> Send someone here right now.</i>

121
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:33,633
<i> I need to get out of here.</i>

122
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:38,267
[REVVING]

123
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:42,467
Let's go straight
to the warehouse.

124
00:05:43,133 --> 00:05:44,967
Are you sure
you want to get off here?

125
00:05:46,067 --> 00:05:48,000
Yes, Yevtte, I'm okay here.

126
00:05:48,133 --> 00:05:51,133
Thank you again,
Boss Idol Andrew.

127
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:57,133
At least I can somehow make up
for what I did to your family.

128
00:05:59,733 --> 00:06:04,467
Miss Clarissa, I'm sorry
if I hurt you.

129
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:09,567
You only did that because you
were angry at the police.

130
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,867
That's what my daughter
Joey told me.

131
00:06:15,233 --> 00:06:18,000
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:06:18,133 --> 00:06:19,167
Actually, what I want to do

133
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,367
is prove that

134
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:24,000
I was wrong about Major Miguel.

135
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,100
And when that happens,

136
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:30,233
I'll be the first one
to report the whole truth.

137
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:33,000
I'm sure you will.

138
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:36,800
I know you, and you always tell
the truth.

139
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,167
But for now, Clarissa
and I will head home.

140
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:43,133
We'll go ahead,
and you should too.

141
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:44,800
It's okay.

142
00:06:44,933 --> 00:06:46,567
Take care.

143
00:06:47,633 --> 00:06:52,033
[PHONE BUZZING]

144
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:54,200
- Hello, Andrew?
- Hello, Joey?

145
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,467
Where are you?

146
00:06:56,967 --> 00:06:58,267
Are you safe?

147
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,733
Yes.
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:06:59,867 --> 00:07:01,833
But why are you
only contacting me now?

149
00:07:01,967 --> 00:07:03,267
I've been calling you
for a while.

150
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,333
<i> How's Mom?</i>

151
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:05,933
Well, they're safe.

152
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:08,333
She's on her way home
with my sister.

153
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,233
That's good.

154
00:07:11,767 --> 00:07:12,867
All right, go back here now.

155
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,467
We need you.

156
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,300
Why? Is there a problem?

157
00:07:16,433 --> 00:07:18,333
Just hurry up.

158
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:26,933
Where's Joey?

159
00:07:27,067 --> 00:07:28,533
- I have the same question.
- Oh...

160
00:07:28,667 --> 00:07:29,633
Oh, looks like these two
are already here.

161
00:07:29,767 --> 00:07:30,700
So?

162
00:07:30,833 --> 00:07:32,767
Did you catch Theresa?

163
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:36,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:38,433
I lost her.

165
00:07:38,567 --> 00:07:42,233
TOTGA, the one that got away.

166
00:07:43,867 --> 00:07:46,600
We didn't gain anything
from this mission.

167
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:47,933
Wrong...

168
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,200
We still got something.

169
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:56,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,867
Let me go!

171
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,767
What the hell?

172
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:12,167
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,400
Sir...

174
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:18,767
Sir, we will just use
the restroom.

175
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,567
Stand there, stay there.

176
00:08:24,433 --> 00:08:25,800
Miguel.

177
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,833
Trigger wants to
talk to you tomorrow.

178
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:31,967
And then, you will
gang up on me again?

179
00:08:32,367 --> 00:08:33,833
Think whatever you want.

180
00:08:33,967 --> 00:08:36,133
That's just what
he told me to say.

181
00:08:36,533 --> 00:08:39,367
It's up to you
whether you go or not.

182
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,033
Hey Miguel, aren't you done yet?

184
00:08:43,167 --> 00:08:44,167
Hurry up!

185
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:46,033
You guys, aren't you done
using the restroom yet?

186
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:46,933
All done.

187
00:08:47,067 --> 00:08:48,933
- Okay, okay, Sir.
- Okay.

188
00:08:49,067 --> 00:08:50,300
Sir.

189
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:54,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:59,600
Let me get out of here!

191
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:01,267
What the hell?

192
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,933
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:09:03,067 --> 00:09:04,733
Why is she here?

194
00:09:06,433 --> 00:09:08,633
How did you capture Golda?

195
00:09:12,067 --> 00:09:13,633
- [SHRIEKS]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

196
00:09:15,133 --> 00:09:16,033
[GROANS]

197
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:17,767
<i>- Miss...
- Are you okay?</i>

198
00:09:19,633 --> 00:09:21,033
<i> Golda?</i>

199
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:24,033
That's why
we brought Golda here.

200
00:09:24,167 --> 00:09:26,000
You tricked me!

201
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:27,367
Not really.

202
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,967
So stop acting up.

203
00:09:29,133 --> 00:09:30,267
Exactly.

204
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,633
You asked us to help you get
away from there, didn't you?

205
00:09:32,767 --> 00:09:34,467
Well, that's exactly
what we did.

206
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,467
You haven't even said
thank you yet.

207
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,700
But there's something else
I want to hear,

208
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:39,533
not just thank you.

209
00:09:39,667 --> 00:09:40,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,900
We already helped you.

211
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:44,133
So can you...

212
00:09:44,267 --> 00:09:45,333
tell me everything you know

213
00:09:45,467 --> 00:09:47,467
about how my father was set up.

214
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,200
Start from the beginning.

215
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:52,967
And don't leave any detail.

216
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:55,500
Yes, yes, what they said.

217
00:09:58,100 --> 00:09:59,667
Start talking.

218
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,000
All the transactions
happen at the spa.

219
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:05,700
And Loloy,

220
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:08,133
he was my contact

221
00:10:08,267 --> 00:10:10,067
who delivered the supplies.

222
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:13,667
Supplies meaning drugs?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:10:17,733 --> 00:10:20,000
And that's where
your father caught me.

224
00:10:21,167 --> 00:10:23,767
But instead of throwing me
in jail,

225
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:27,000
he made me his informant
in exchange for my freedom.

226
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,633
But...

227
00:10:29,767 --> 00:10:31,567
but Parak found out.

228
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,300
Godfather Diego.

229
00:10:33,433 --> 00:10:34,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,233
<i>I was just cornered,
that's why I gave the tip.</i>

231
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:40,733
<i>I'm sorry, Diego,
I'll keep quiet...</i>

232
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:42,633
<i> just please don't kill me.</i>

233
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,433
<i>I don't want you to stay quiet.</i>

234
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:46,300
<i>What I want is for you to sing.</i>

235
00:10:46,433 --> 00:10:48,767
<i> And I'll dictate the lyrics.</i>

236
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,867
He threatened me!

237
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
He threatened me,
that's why...

238
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:56,100
I started making up stories
to ruin Miguel.

239
00:10:57,233 --> 00:10:58,267
Then...

240
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,367
when Miguel was imprisoned,

241
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,367
that's when I went into hiding

242
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,600
because I knew...

243
00:11:03,733 --> 00:11:06,267
I knew I'd be next for Berdugo.

244
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,033
Berdugo?

245
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,767
He's the leader
of the syndicates.

246
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:14,067
How about Theresa Park or Lisa?

247
00:11:15,767 --> 00:11:18,833
I don't know anyone
named Lisa or Theresa.

248
00:11:20,033 --> 00:11:22,967
The only one I know is Loloy.

249
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:24,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:11:24,733 --> 00:11:27,333
Most likely, Berdugo was the one
who set your father up.

251
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:29,333
Then who is Berdugo?

252
00:11:29,467 --> 00:11:31,033
What's his real name?

253
00:11:32,267 --> 00:11:33,900
Nothing, I don't know.

254
00:11:34,033 --> 00:11:35,367
I've never even talked to him.

255
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,067
I've never seen him in person,

256
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,167
not even on the phone,
I never talked to him.

257
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,933
Can you stop lying!

258
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,600
Admit everything!

259
00:11:42,733 --> 00:11:44,333
I'm not lying to you!

260
00:11:44,467 --> 00:11:47,500
What do you want? I already told
you everything I know!

261
00:11:47,633 --> 00:11:48,700
If you don't want to believe me,

262
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,967
then that's your problem!

263
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,300
You know what,
we're all exhausted.

264
00:11:53,433 --> 00:11:55,133
So much happened tonight.

265
00:11:55,267 --> 00:11:57,933
Maybe it's better
if we just rest.

266
00:11:58,067 --> 00:12:00,400
Joey, I'll talk to you tomorrow.

267
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:03,067
I'll watch Golda,
I'll handle it.

268
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,933
Let's get some rest.

269
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:09,067
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:12:11,633 --> 00:12:13,667
Golda, are you there?

271
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:17,667
Where else would I go, huh?

272
00:12:18,067 --> 00:12:19,733
Just making sure.

273
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,600
Is she not done yet?
I still need to talk to her.

274
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:34,900
Joey...

275
00:12:36,167 --> 00:12:38,767
I think it would be better if
I'm the one who talks to Golda

276
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,167
so she can become our witness.

277
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:12:42,733 --> 00:12:45,600
Why again?
Because I'm emotional right now.

279
00:12:45,733 --> 00:12:49,267
Well, obviously my anger
comes from somewhere.

280
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:50,533
Yes, there is.

281
00:12:50,667 --> 00:12:52,500
And we all know that.

282
00:12:53,067 --> 00:12:56,467
She ruined your father
and your whole family.

283
00:12:57,033 --> 00:13:00,367
But we have to strategize
to get Golda on our side.

284
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:01,833
Yeah, he's right.

285
00:13:01,967 --> 00:13:05,167
Scaring and antagonizing her
won't be helpful.

286
00:13:07,367 --> 00:13:08,500
Okay, fine.

287
00:13:08,633 --> 00:13:10,900
For Dad's sake,
I won't go after her.

288
00:13:11,033 --> 00:13:13,967
Just make sure she cooperates.

289
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:18,333
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:13:23,867 --> 00:13:27,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

291
00:13:29,567 --> 00:13:32,633
-[KNOCK]
-Golda, what are you doing?

292
00:13:33,733 --> 00:13:35,833
- [KNOCKS]
- Golda.

293
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,500
- [KNOCKS]
- Hey.

294
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:42,000
I'm just going to take a shower,
okay?

295
00:13:44,367 --> 00:13:45,900
Okay.

296
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:56,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:14:02,333 --> 00:14:07,767
[PHONE RINGING]

298
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,167
Oh, Joey, how are you?

299
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:12,433
<i>Hello, Mom?
How are you?</i>

300
00:14:12,567 --> 00:14:13,600
I'm okay.

301
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:15,567
Oh! Joey...

302
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:18,733
<i>You won't believe what happened
to me last night.</i>

303
00:14:18,867 --> 00:14:20,900
I almost died!

304
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:23,533
What? How?

305
00:14:23,967 --> 00:14:27,367
My boss brought me to a party,

306
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:28,467
<i> then chaos broke out.</i>

307
00:14:28,633 --> 00:14:31,100
There was an actual shootout.

308
00:14:31,233 --> 00:14:32,300
We didn't know

309
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:35,433
that the one who invited us was
part of a syndicate.

310
00:14:35,567 --> 00:14:36,833
<i> But...</i>

311
00:14:36,967 --> 00:14:38,933
someone saved me, Boss Budol...

312
00:14:39,067 --> 00:14:40,567
I mean...

313
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,567
<i> Boss Idol.</i>

314
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:43,733
Do you remember
my boss's brother?

315
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,433
Ah...

316
00:14:47,567 --> 00:14:49,400
You weren't hurt, Mom?

317
00:14:49,533 --> 00:14:51,300
No, child, I'm safe.

318
00:14:51,433 --> 00:14:54,167
Andrew saved me.

319
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,067
Ah...

320
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,400
And you know what,

321
00:14:56,533 --> 00:14:58,467
he apologized to me

322
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:02,100
for what he did
to your father, to us.

323
00:15:02,267 --> 00:15:05,700
I could see and feel
his sincerity.

324
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,033
He's actually kind, isn't he?

325
00:15:09,167 --> 00:15:10,833
<i> And brave.</i>

326
00:15:10,967 --> 00:15:12,200
<i> You know,</i>

327
00:15:12,333 --> 00:15:14,000
<i> he never left my side</i>

328
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:16,600
<i>even though his sister
was there.</i>

329
00:15:25,433 --> 00:15:27,200
- This is crazy.
- We're already hungry.

330
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:28,633
What a shameless.

331
00:15:28,767 --> 00:15:38,733
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

332
00:15:47,067 --> 00:15:49,200
What is this, cellmate?

333
00:15:49,333 --> 00:15:50,367
Is this all we get?

334
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,600
That's enough, that's enough.
Break it up, break it up.

335
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:57,033
That's enough, that's enough.

336
00:15:57,167 --> 00:15:58,867
Stop! Stop!

337
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,333
- Stop! Stop!
- That's too much, Sir!

338
00:16:04,667 --> 00:16:06,267
What do you want?

339
00:16:08,267 --> 00:16:11,167
You're the one I'm asking
what you need.

340
00:16:14,033 --> 00:16:15,933
You saved my life, right?

341
00:16:16,967 --> 00:16:19,800
In return,
I'll give you one favor.

342
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:24,167
Only one?

343
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,467
Nothing unlimited here.

344
00:16:30,833 --> 00:16:31,600
So if I were you,

345
00:16:31,733 --> 00:16:33,967
think carefully
about what you want.

346
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:36,667
I'll come back for your answer,
think about it.

347
00:16:44,133 --> 00:16:45,567
Let's eat!

348
00:16:47,633 --> 00:16:51,000
Sorry, this is all
I managed to prepare.

349
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,233
We didn't really have food here.

350
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,267
Just for lunch,
I'll make it up next time.

351
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,833
Come on.

352
00:16:56,967 --> 00:16:58,433
It's fine.

353
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:01,500
Thanks for preparing this.

354
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,500
Hey, Peter!

355
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:07,233
Let's eat.

356
00:17:07,367 --> 00:17:08,533
Go ahead.

357
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:10,933
The one I'm watching still
hasn't come out.

358
00:17:11,067 --> 00:17:12,867
I'll wait for Golda.

359
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:18,767
Joey...

360
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:21,033
I'm just going outside
for a bit.

361
00:17:21,167 --> 00:17:31,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:57,533
Where are you going?

363
00:17:57,667 --> 00:18:01,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

364
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:02,567
What is this?

365
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:05,033
Why are you doing this?

366
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,600
Do you know that
what you're doing to me

367
00:18:06,733 --> 00:18:08,000
is illegal detention?

368
00:18:08,133 --> 00:18:10,000
I'll report you!

369
00:18:10,467 --> 00:18:12,067
To whom?

370
00:18:12,767 --> 00:18:14,233
To the police?

371
00:18:15,367 --> 00:18:17,000
Go! Do it.

372
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,567
Just make sure no one is waiting
for you outside.

373
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,200
And pray...

374
00:18:23,333 --> 00:18:27,867
that the cop you run to isn't
under Berdugo or Godfather.

375
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:31,533
Yes, I know.

376
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:34,033
Godfather is angry at you

377
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:35,900
and he's having you hunted.

378
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:39,233
Why is he mad at me, huh?

379
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:40,967
I didn't do anything wrong.

380
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,867
I didn't double-cross them.

381
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,667
I swear!

382
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:48,833
Even that Braganza guy
is probably blaming me.

383
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:51,300
He didn't even let me explain.

384
00:18:51,433 --> 00:18:53,533
Why? Do you think...

385
00:18:53,667 --> 00:18:54,967
if you meet them in person

386
00:18:55,133 --> 00:18:57,033
they'll listen to you?

387
00:18:57,167 --> 00:19:00,100
They might just delete you
permanently.

388
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:04,933
You know what kind of people
they are, Golda.

389
00:19:05,867 --> 00:19:09,100
You know what they're capable
of doing.

390
00:19:13,867 --> 00:19:15,800
Golda, all of them
are looking for you.

391
00:19:17,133 --> 00:19:20,400
All of them want you dead.

392
00:19:21,467 --> 00:19:24,233
Actually, Joey and I are
the only incentive

393
00:19:24,367 --> 00:19:26,100
to stay alive.

394
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,100
So if I were you,

395
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:32,267
I'd really think about
whose side I'm on.

396
00:19:41,667 --> 00:19:43,467
You eat first.

397
00:19:56,133 --> 00:19:57,633
I think she escaped.

398
00:19:57,767 --> 00:19:59,000
What? How?

399
00:19:59,133 --> 00:20:01,533
She must have gone
through the window!

400
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,000
No, I thought she was just
taking a shower.

401
00:20:03,133 --> 00:20:04,433
The shower is still running.

402
00:20:04,567 --> 00:20:06,267
Come on, let's find her!

403
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,467
Let's go!

404
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,033
Jin Ho!

405
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:20,667
You really thought you could
slip past us, huh?

406
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:23,067
You've got some nerve!

407
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,600
Good thing you saw her.

408
00:20:24,733 --> 00:20:26,233
Of course.

409
00:20:26,367 --> 00:20:28,800
And she's willing
to be our witness.

410
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,933
All right, fine.

411
00:20:32,733 --> 00:20:34,800
Just don't tie me up.

412
00:20:34,967 --> 00:20:38,900
And make sure I'm safe
from the people hunting me.

413
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:40,967
I don't want to die yet.

414
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:43,200
If you're just saying that
to trick us,

415
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:44,433
we'll be the ones to tell

416
00:20:44,567 --> 00:20:46,633
the people you're hiding from
where you are.

417
00:20:48,633 --> 00:20:49,700
This is the only thing
I'm asking in return

418
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:52,200
for everything you did
to my family.

419
00:20:52,667 --> 00:20:54,567
So you should cooperate.

420
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:57,133
No more running, no more tricks.

421
00:21:15,167 --> 00:21:17,633
Godfather and Braganza
are now feuding.

422
00:21:17,767 --> 00:21:19,000
The two of them are going
to kill each other.

423
00:21:19,133 --> 00:21:20,933
But what you're asking is
difficult.

424
00:21:21,067 --> 00:21:22,400
It's hard to find Berdugo.

425
00:21:22,533 --> 00:21:24,000
No one stays hidden forever.

426
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:25,833
According to our
reliable source,

427
00:21:25,967 --> 00:21:28,333
the wanted drug dealer
in Bolagos

428
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:29,900
is known by the name Loloy.

429
00:21:30,033 --> 00:21:32,567
We need to find out
who the whistleblower is.

430
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:33,833
Tell me, who is your source?

431
00:21:33,967 --> 00:21:36,200
Brother, you know
I don't burn my sources.

432
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:38,567
Besides, you won't be
involved anyway...

433
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,367
unless you're doing
something illegal.

434
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,533
Didn't he say anything?

435
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:42,833
- He did.
- Golda.

436
00:21:42,967 --> 00:21:44,100
I'll be the one watching you.

437
00:21:44,233 --> 00:21:46,067
Are you really watching me,

438
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,167
or your girlfriend?

439
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:48,600
- Ah...
- Yes.

440
00:21:48,733 --> 00:21:49,800
They're not together!

441
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:52,167
Boss Budol is the one
who scam me!

442
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,967
- Young love.
- My contact said

443
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:56,433
<i>Golda has already given
a statement.</i>

444
00:21:56,567 --> 00:21:58,400
We have to make sure
that her testimony

445
00:21:58,533 --> 00:21:59,600
doesn't see the light of day.

446
00:21:59,733 --> 00:22:01,100
Matias, you know the drill.

447
00:22:01,233 --> 00:22:02,167
Copy, Berdugo.

448
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,933
There's someone,
are they still there?

449
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:04,967
They might break in.

450
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:06,700
Just don't make any noise.
